{{- /*
skip.sh.tmpl — declared early-exit contract for run_onchange_ / run_once_ scripts.

WHY THIS EXISTS. chezmoi records a script that exits 0 as a SUCCESSFUL run and
will not re-run it until its rendered content changes. A script that gave up
because a precondition was missing therefore claims a convergence it never
reached, permanently. Ten lines across six scripts used to print "retries next
apply" from exactly such a path. This partial makes the claim explicit, derives
the behaviour and the message from it, and lets CI reject a site that declares
nothing.

FOUR CALL FORMS. Every conditional early exit in a run_onchange_/run_once_
script goes through one of these — including the ones that are NOT skips. That
total coverage is what makes the guard decidable: after conversion, a bare
`exit 0` or `return 0` on a conditional path is by definition undeclared.

  skip_here       deferred work; exits the script
  skip_step       deferred work; returns non-zero so the caller can `return`
                  and the script continues (fedora's per-function returns,
                  setup-podman-cluster's substeps)
  done_here       the work is already done (a completion stamp). Not deferred.
  not_applicable  deliberately opted out in data, or an all-work-done fast
                  path. Not deferred.

THREE DIRECTIONS, for the two skip forms only:

  harmless             this host will never satisfy the condition, so not
                       acting is correct and final. Exits 0. Nothing is
                       outstanding. Baked host identity (wrong desktop, wrong
                       distro, container) lives here.
  transient-tolerable  an eligible host is missing a precondition AND failing
                       here cannot prevent later work. Exits 1, so chezmoi does
                       NOT record the run and it retries by itself. Only valid
                       when nothing later depends on this script: `chezmoi
                       apply` aborts every subsequent script at the first script
                       error, and `--keep-going` is flag-only (not settable in
                       the config file), so an early-phase exit 1 would strand
                       every later phase.
  transient-blocking   an eligible host is missing a precondition, but exiting
                       non-zero here WOULD abort later phases. Exits 0 and
                       declares a capabilities.tmpl probe, so the rendered
                       content changes when the precondition appears and chezmoi
                       re-runs the script on its own.

WHY A PROBE AND NOT A MARKER FILE. Measured on chezmoi v2.71.0 against a scratch
source and destination: a marker whose content changes on each skip re-runs the
script on EVERY apply (an always-run script); a marker with stable content ran
twice, then stalled permanently and did NOT re-run when the precondition
appeared. Only a render-time probe of the precondition itself is both stable
while the precondition is absent and different once it is present. A
transient-blocking site therefore MUST name a probe, and this partial fails the
render when it does not.

WHY THE DIRECTION IS A RENDER-TIME LITERAL. A template cannot inspect a value a
shell function receives at runtime, so a runtime-argument API could not reject
an unknown direction. Passing the direction as template data is what lets this
partial `fail` the apply on a typo, the same way facts-validate.tmpl does for an
unknown fact name.

ARGUMENT — a dict, never a bare string:

  {{ includeTemplate "skip.sh.tmpl" (dict
       "ctx"       .
       "form"      "skip_here"
       "script"    "config-gnome-app-grid-order"
       "site"      "no-session-bus"
       "direction" "transient-blocking"
       "probe"     "session-bus-present"
       "reason"    "no D-Bus session bus") }}

`script` plus `site` is the stable identity dotfiles-skips reports and clears
on, so `site` must be unique within its script. The emitted shell is
self-contained — no prelude, no shared function to inline first.
*/ -}}
{{- if not (kindIs "map" .) -}}
{{-   fail (printf "skip.sh.tmpl: expected a dict, got a %s (%v). Pass the call as data: {{ includeTemplate \"skip.sh.tmpl\" (dict \"ctx\" . \"form\" \"skip_here\" \"script\" \"my-script\" \"site\" \"my-site\" \"direction\" \"harmless\" \"reason\" \"...\") }}" (kindOf .) .) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- /* chezmoi renders with missingkey=error, so an absent key must be tested
   with hasKey before it is read — `.probe | default ""` errors on the read,
   before default can substitute. */ -}}
{{- $form := "" -}}{{- if hasKey . "form" -}}{{- $form = .form -}}{{- end -}}
{{- $script := "" -}}{{- if hasKey . "script" -}}{{- $script = .script -}}{{- end -}}
{{- $site := "" -}}{{- if hasKey . "site" -}}{{- $site = .site -}}{{- end -}}
{{- $reason := "" -}}{{- if hasKey . "reason" -}}{{- $reason = .reason -}}{{- end -}}
{{- $direction := "" -}}{{- if hasKey . "direction" -}}{{- $direction = .direction -}}{{- end -}}
{{- $probe := "" -}}{{- if hasKey . "probe" -}}{{- $probe = .probe -}}{{- end -}}
{{- $forms := list "skip_here" "skip_step" "done_here" "not_applicable" -}}
{{- if not (has $form $forms) -}}
{{-   fail (printf "skip.sh.tmpl: unknown form %q for %s/%s. Valid forms: skip_here, skip_step, done_here, not_applicable." $form $script $site) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- if eq $script "" -}}
{{-   fail (printf "skip.sh.tmpl: %q call is missing \"script\". It is half of the stable identity dotfiles-skips reports on." $form) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- if eq $site "" -}}
{{-   fail (printf "skip.sh.tmpl: %q call in %s is missing \"site\". It must be unique within the script so a later run can clear exactly this entry." $form $script) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- if eq $reason "" -}}
{{-   fail (printf "skip.sh.tmpl: %q call %s/%s is missing \"reason\". The operator-facing message is derived from it." $form $script $site) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $isSkip := or (eq $form "skip_here") (eq $form "skip_step") -}}
{{- $directions := list "harmless" "transient-tolerable" "transient-blocking" -}}
{{- if $isSkip -}}
{{-   if not (has $direction $directions) -}}
{{-     fail (printf "skip.sh.tmpl: unknown direction %q for %s/%s. Valid directions: harmless, transient-tolerable, transient-blocking." $direction $script $site) -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{-   if and (eq $direction "transient-blocking") (eq $probe "") -}}
{{-     fail (printf "skip.sh.tmpl: %s/%s is transient-blocking but names no \"probe\". Without a capabilities.tmpl probe hashed into this script's fingerprint, the skip is recorded as a successful run and never re-runs. Name a probe, or reclassify the site." $script $site) -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{-   if and (ne $direction "transient-blocking") (ne $probe "") -}}
{{-     fail (printf "skip.sh.tmpl: %s/%s declares probe %q but is %s. Only transient-blocking consumes a probe." $script $site $probe $direction) -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{- else -}}
{{-   if ne $direction "" -}}
{{-     fail (printf "skip.sh.tmpl: %s/%s uses form %q, which takes no direction (it is not deferred work). Drop \"direction\", or use skip_here / skip_step." $script $site $form) -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $dir := "\"${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/chezmoi/skips\"" -}}
{{- $file := printf "\"${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/chezmoi/skips/%s__%s\"" $script $site -}}
{{- if eq $form "done_here" }}
printf '%s: %s\n' {{ $script | quote }} {{ printf "%s; nothing to do" $reason | quote }}
rm -f {{ $file }} 2>/dev/null || true
exit 0
{{- else if eq $form "not_applicable" }}
printf '%s: %s\n' {{ $script | quote }} {{ printf "%s; not applicable on this host" $reason | quote }}
rm -f {{ $file }} 2>/dev/null || true
exit 0
{{- else if eq $direction "harmless" }}
printf '%s: %s\n' {{ $script | quote }} {{ $reason | quote }}
rm -f {{ $file }} 2>/dev/null || true
{{ if eq $form "skip_here" }}exit 0{{ else }}return 1{{ end }}
{{- else if eq $direction "transient-tolerable" }}
printf '%s: %s. Not recorded as done; the next apply retries it.\n' {{ $script | quote }} {{ $reason | quote }} >&2
mkdir -p {{ $dir }} 2>/dev/null || true
printf 'v1\t%s\t%s\t%s\t%s\n' {{ $script | quote }} {{ $site | quote }} 'transient-tolerable' {{ $reason | quote }} \
  > {{ $file }} 2>/dev/null || true
{{ if eq $form "skip_here" }}exit 1{{ else }}return 1{{ end }}
{{- else }}
printf '%s: %s. Recorded as done; it re-runs automatically once %s changes.\n' {{ $script | quote }} {{ $reason | quote }} {{ $probe | quote }}
mkdir -p {{ $dir }} 2>/dev/null || true
printf 'v1\t%s\t%s\t%s\t%s\n' {{ $script | quote }} {{ $site | quote }} {{ printf "transient-blocking:%s" $probe | quote }} {{ $reason | quote }} \
  > {{ $file }} 2>/dev/null || true
{{ if eq $form "skip_here" }}exit 0{{ else }}return 1{{ end }}
{{- end }}
